{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791037805,"nonce":"IpnPJnr0D1EpYjcdtfP1zndOVtE=","message":"Both halves done: 673f3244 for signal(), e7a55968 for computed().\n\nsignal() was the straightforward half, as the analysis above expected. computed() was not, and the reason matters more than the fix: get_derived took `\u0026node.compute as *const _`, a raw pointer INTO the derived map, and held it across the compute call. read_derived_in_flight held a reference across the same call. So inserting a derived mid-evaluation would not have panicked, it could have reallocated the slotmap under a live pointer. A use-after-free, not a deadlock.\n\nSo the fix is not interior mutability alone. with_compute takes the closure out of the node, calls it with the map unborrowed, and a Drop guard puts it back even if it panics. DerivedNode.compute became Option\u003cComputeFn\u003e for that.\n\nThree borrow-across-callback hazards fixed on the way, each of which would have panicked once the maps became RefCells:\n- set() held its borrow across mark_dirty and flush_effects, which run user closures that may now create.\n- mark_dirty recursed while borrowing the derived map.\n- get_derived's subscription bookkeeping borrowed both maps at once.\n\nOne behaviour change worth knowing: a derived mid-evaluation has no closure in the map, so a nested read of the SAME derived answers None instead of recursing. Pinned by a test, since it would otherwise look like a bug.\n\nSeven tests. Each was checked by removing the in-flight path and confirming it HANGS rather than fails, with a timeout so the check did not block. 1429 workspace tests pass; clippy, fmt and rustdoc clean.\n\nEffects are still not creatable in flight: run_effect takes a raw pointer into the effects map the same way, and EffectNode.run is FnMut, so take-and-restore needs more care than the Fn case. Nobody has asked for it.","files":null}]}